# BUGS

The trusted keys last as long as 9gate does: they aren't kept on disk.

There is no way to end a listener or an import but to restart 9gate.

A plain listener's only protection is its callers' addresses, which anyone on the link can take: use it on a network you trust, and allow as little as you can.
It is held to its address by 9gate, not by the stack, so a call to another address of the node is answered, then hung up.
